% c572 (A&S Unit 17, PDF 266-268, Ex. 17-3a): 33 the basses touch A1 under the winds' call on iv, as they touch E1 under the call at 29 and G1 at 37,
%   so the counterstatement's descending fifths E-A-D-G are all in the bass register and the low line B1 (32) - A1 (33) - G1 (37) steps down (one of the series' two stepwise lines, brought out by register).
sACb = { e,,4\p r4 r4 | e,,4 r4 r4 | e,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | e,,4 r4 r4 | a,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | e,,4 r4 r4 | a,,4 r4 r4 | gis,,4 r4 r4 | a,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | e,,4 r4 r4 | g,,4 r4 a,,4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | e,,4 r4 r4 | e,,4\pp r4 r4 | R2. | e,,2.\pp^\markup \italic "arco" | b,,2. | a,,4-. r4 r4 | R2. | d,2.~ | d,2. | g,,4-.\p\< r4 r4 | g,,4-. r4 r4 | g,,4-. r4 r4 | d,4-. r4 r4 | d,4-.\f r4 r4 | d,4-. r4 r4 | d,4-. r4 r4 | R2. | g,,2(\f g,4~ | g,4 b,,2) | d,2( e,4~ | e,4 gis,,2) | a,,2(\< a,4~ | a,4 cis,2) | e,2( d,4~ | d,4 cis,2) | d,2.~\ff | d,2. | g,,2. | g,,4-. r4 r4 | }
% c084: 45 Hn 1 B4 (was D5) and Hn 1-2 mf (were f): the held horn D5 at f sat on the accented first note of the tune's lower octave (Ob 1 mf, Vln II) and covered it;
%   forte brass have the densest spectrum and come to the front, and sounds in one frequency band mask each other (Casanelles PDF 275, 287, 289; Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 108, 112).
% c067: 45 Fl 1 mf under Vln I's f espress. (it doubles the violins at the unison up to A6; Sebesky PDF 164: the flute on the lead violin line a degree softer).
% c445: 45 (Vln I, Vln II, Vla) up-bow written \upb (global.ily): with \upbow the score dropped the 45-46 slur and the B tie (Adler I PDF 37).
% c575: 49, c485's override on Vln I's D6 replaced by \beatq #-0.4 (global.ily): beat 1-2-2½-3 now 2.99/1.99/4.03 spaces (was 3.01/1.46/4.04; the 4.03 holds the sharps of beat 3); the dotted crotchet keeps more space than the quaver (Gould PDF 54). Print only.
